  "description": "SPB runtime file mirror list. Root-level files and selected asset directories are the source of truth; they are copied into every entry in `targets`. See scripts/README.md and scripts/RUNTIME_SYNC.md. 2026-04-21 HEENAN OVERNIGHT post-Codex-audit: extended to include the 4 hot-path Python modules that were previously only mirrored at Electron build time via electron-app/copy-server-assets.js. The Codex audit of the overnight loop found that Python backend edits did not reach the Electron runtime per-edit, only per-build; this manifest now covers both paths so `node scripts/sync-runtime-copies.js --write` catches them. 2026-04-22 HEENAN FAMILY overnight iter 4 (Foundation trust): added engine/base_registry_data.py so Foundation-Base metadata edits at root auto-sync to Electron mirrors (previously only copied at build-time, caused recurrent drift). 2026-05-05 cultural texture fix: added directory mirroring for image-authored Cultural finishes so Viva Mexico / Rising Sun texture packs cannot disappear from the served Electron runtime. 2026-06-09 (3->2 COPY): REMOVED the third mirror electron-app/server/pyserver/_internal \u2014 it was a vestigial PyInstaller bundle EXCLUDED from the installer (package.json !pyserver/**), so it shipped to nobody and only created 3-way drift risk. Sync is now 2-copy: repo root -> electron-app/server ONLY. See CHANGELOG 2026-06-09. 2026-09-04 ROOT CLEANUP: removed SPB_AUDIT_anime/relics/xlab_shift.html from the mirror list. They are regenerable owner review pages (verdicts live in _audit/*.json), no route serves them, and electron-builder's extraResources filter did NOT exclude them - so ~40 MB of audit pages were being copied into every customer installer. Archived to _archive/root_cleanup_2026-09-04/audit_pages/.",
